; wd2l, container mode (Quadlet): the containers write /var/lib/wd2l (state.json, spool/) with
; this label, instead of Podman's :z, which would also relabel the receiver's capture archive
; (/var/lib/wd2l/pcap, netutils_tmp_t, receiver/wd2l_pcap.cil) and stop host tcpdump writing
; it. The more specific pcap rule still wins. The block needs container-selinux
; (container_file_t): on a host without it, it stays off and nothing changes. It adds no
; permission to any domain. The wd2l RPM loads it (semodule) and relabels the directory.
(optional wd2l_container_files
  (filecon "/var/lib/wd2l(/.*)?" any (system_u object_r container_file_t ((s0) (s0)))))
